.TH std::philox_engine::set_counter 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::philox_engine::set_counter \- std::philox_engine::set_counter

.SH Synopsis
void set_counter( const std::array<result_type, n>& c );  (since C++26)

Sets the counter of the random-number engine.

  * For each integer k in [0, n), sets \\(\\scriptsize X_k \\)Xk to \\(\\scriptsize c_{n-1-k}
    \\mod 2^w \\)cn-1-k mod 2w
    .
  * The value of j is set to n - 1.^[1]
 1. ↑ As j is being set to n - 1, the next state transition always generates new random
    values.

.SH Parameters

c - counter sequence to use to set the counter

.SH Complexity

\\(\\scriptsize O(n) \\)O(n).

.SH See also

constructor   constructs the engine
              \fI(public member function)\fP
seed          sets the current state of the engine
              \fI(public member function)\fP
